WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.420
At a synapse, a chemical message crosses the
gap to the next cell in under a millisecond.

2
00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:08.440
A hormone works differently.

3
00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:12.650
It's carried in the blood, and
reaches almost every cell in the body.

4
00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:16.450
Every one of those cells is
bathed in the same hormone.

5
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:18.700
Yet only a few respond.

6
00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:22.220
So how does a cell pick
which messages to answer?

7
00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:26.330
In this mission, you'll compare
three ways cells send messages:

8
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:30.380
by touch, across a tiny
gap, and through the blood.

9
00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:34.540
Then you'll zoom in on the moment
a messenger molecule meets a cell,

10
00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:36.640
and see what changes shape.

11
00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:40.990
Your mission: find out how a cell
picks which messages to answer.
